{"id":"cec14c92b8acd1221e70e81dc41c8f58b46e7030","axis":"silent","repo":"graphql/graphql-js","sha":"cec14c92b8acd1221e70e81dc41c8f58b46e7030","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".github/CONTRIBUTING.md","lines":["@@ -111,16 +111,18 @@ change website API output must include the generated files."," "," ### Executable API examples"," ","-Run `npm run check:examples` to execute all JavaScript and TypeScript fences under","-JSDoc `@example` tags in `src`. No package build is needed. CI runs the same check","-on the latest supported Node.js version.","-","-Each fence is a separate ES module: include its imports and setup. The runner","-rewrites imports and assertion comments, strips types with Node, and executes","-the code directly in memory. Imports from `graphql` resolve directly to the","-source in `src`.","-It checks runtime behavior, not TypeScript types. GraphQL fences are not executed.","-Examples without expectations are smoke tests.","+Run `npm run check:examples` to execute JSDoc `@example` code fences in `src`","+against the built npm package. CI runs the same check on the latest supported","+Node.js version.","+","+Executable examples must use TypeScript, with a `ts` or `typescript` fence.","+Each fence is a separate ES module: include its imports and setup. All examples","+are type checked against the built package before execution, using the","+repository's TypeScript settings except `noUnusedLocals`. Examples must both","+type check and run successfully. Use optional chaining for optional values or","+`assert` to check and narrow required values, rather than non-null assertions.","+Only `graphql` and `gql` fences are excluded from execution. Examples without","+expectations are still type checked and run as smoke tests."," "," Add a fenced example under `@example` in the API's JSDoc comment. Use trailing"," comments to describe expected results:","@@ -152,6 +154,7 @@ kind.toLowerCase(); // => 'document'"," "," Use one initialized variable declaration per annotatio